From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:42:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] nvme-pci: Bring Apple ANS controllers up from reset_work
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

nvme_probe() enables the controller synchronously, and nvme-pci probes
in the async domain that kernel_init() waits for before it runs /init.
On the A9 iPad an ANS bring-up that hung, or waited out CAP.TO (minutes),
therefore kept the initramfs from ever starting, and nothing in
userspace could report the storage failure.

For Apple ANS, queue the first enable on nvme_reset_wq instead, as
nvme-pci did before it became synchronous: probe returns once the BAR is
mapped, reset_work allocates the admin tag set on its first run and does
the rest. A failure leaves the controller dead instead of blocking boot.
Other controllers are unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
[Orchard: from brkosebay/linux 1e342d43 (J71t ledger 3.7); the
 "continues in the background" message dropped, otherwise as is]
Co-developed-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Signed-off-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/nvme/host/pci.c | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/nvme/host/pci.c b/drivers/nvme/host/pci.c
index ff463ccbb..257174534 100644
--- a/drivers/nvme/host/pci.c
+++ b/drivers/nvme/host/pci.c
@@ -3395,6 +3395,15 @@ static void nvme_reset_work(struct work_struct *work)
 	result = nvme_pci_enable(dev);
 	if (result)
 		goto out_unlock;
+	if (!dev->ctrl.admin_q) {
+		/* First enable, deferred from nvme_probe() (Apple ANS) */
+		result = nvme_alloc_admin_tag_set(&dev->ctrl,
+						  &dev->admin_tagset,
+						  &nvme_mq_admin_ops,
+						  sizeof(struct nvme_iod));
+		if (result)
+			goto out_unlock;
+	}
 	nvme_unquiesce_admin_queue(&dev->ctrl);
 	mutex_unlock(&dev->shutdown_lock);
 
@@ -3770,6 +3779,24 @@ static int nvme_probe(struct pci_dev *pdev, const struct pci_device_id *id)
 
 	dev_info(dev->ctrl.device, "pci function %s\n", dev_name(&pdev->dev));
 
+	/*
+	 * Apple ANS: do the first enable from reset_work, as nvme-pci did before
+	 * it became synchronous. The probe runs in the async domain that
+	 * kernel_init() waits for before it starts /init, and an ANS bring-up
+	 * that hangs or waits out CAP.TO (minutes) would otherwise keep
+	 * userspace from starting and reporting the failure.
+	 */
+	if (dev->dma_ops == &nvme_pci_apple_ans_ops) {
+		if (!nvme_change_ctrl_state(&dev->ctrl, NVME_CTRL_RESETTING)) {
+			result = -EBUSY;
+			goto out_release_iod_mempool;
+		}
+		pci_set_drvdata(pdev, dev);
+		queue_work(nvme_reset_wq, &dev->ctrl.reset_work);
+		nvme_put_ctrl(&dev->ctrl);
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	result = nvme_pci_enable(dev);
 	if (result)
 		goto out_release_iod_mempool;
